; Office's own verbose logging, the switch Microsoft's own
; troubleshooting guide asks for ("Enable enterprise logging for
; Microsoft 365 Apps"): EnableLogging under the user's
; Office\16.0\Common\Logging, which Word reads on startup, and the
; Click-to-Run override's LogLevel and PipelineLogging. All three keys
; are in office_word's ledger as absent. The logs land in %TEMP% as
; MachineName-Date-time.log, which is why the scenario dumps the user's
; Temp. Loaded after registry.seed (module string `registry`).

[\Registry\User\S-1-5-21-1000000001-1000000002-1000000003-1001\Software\Microsoft\Office\16.0\Common\Logging]
"EnableLogging"=dword:1

[\Registry\Machine\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\ClickToRun\OverRide]
"LogLevel"=dword:3
"PipelineLogging"=dword:1
